            <div xml:id="d496">

                <pb facs="0777" n="651" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg651"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5045/63: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cunningham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-06-04T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 4, 1925—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 4—8:33 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>New developments today include strike of dining-room boys, Astor House and some
                    other hotels, Shanghai club and domestic servants. Strike seems to be extending
                    and is certainly more effective.</p>
                <p>Chinese Chamber of Commerce is now approaching foreign chambers of commerce to
                    bring about better conditions.</p>
                <p>Great Eastern and Burlington Hotels were searched this morning and considerable
                    Bolshevik literature and munitions was [<hi rendition="#italic">were</hi>] found
                    in certain rooms. All public wharves expecting [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >excepting?</hi>] Dollar and Jardine Matheson are closed on account of
                    strike. Chinese banks have been closed for 2 days.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
